From 07ca49a65caf36f85a077aec8e2299cc2d2ebcb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:29:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 092/294] pco: branch over uniform if bodies and compare
 straight into p0

Every if was lowered with the execution mask counter (cndst, br.allinst,
cndef, br.allinst, cndend), even when all instances take the same side.
The descriptor check versioning puts such an if at the top of most
shaders, so the fast path paid 8 control instructions.

An if whose condition is computed only by pure ALU ops from shared
registers, constants and immediates, with no loop or masking if around it,
now sets p0 with an (ignorepe) test and branches over the body that is not
taken. The condition producers become (ignorepe) too, so p0 is valid in
every instance. A large uniform body is branched over rather than issued
predicated. The emc is now initialised at the start of the function, so
it is set on every path.

New op tstp compares two sources into a predicate. If prologues recompute
a bcmp condition straight into p0 instead of testing its boolean result;
DCE removes the bcmp when nothing else uses it.

glmark2 (zink, off-screen) vs before: function +4..6%, conditionals
+6..9%, loop +4..8%, jellyfish +7%. The function fragment shader's fast
path goes from 8 control instructions to 2.
